From: REIMU <reimu@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: aspeed-vhub: remote wakeup: an edge each time

ast_vhub_send_host_wakeup() sets VHUB_CTRL_MANUAL_REMOTE_WAKEUP and nothing
ever clears it. When the host has suspended the hub (USB autosuspend of the
hub with nothing on its ports, remote wakeup enabled) and a gadget then
connects to a port, ast_vhub_device_connect() asks for a wakeup; on the
REIMU-5564 board the host never woke (its "usb 4-4: usb auto-suspend,
wakeup 1" stayed, the HID gadget never enumerated). If the hardware acts on
the bit going from 0 to 1, every wakeup after the first one is lost: clear
it before setting it, and once the bus has resumed. Harmless if the
hardware clears it itself. Same code in 5.10.

Not verified on the hardware: on the board, a "devmem 0x1e6a0000" with bit 4
set while the hub runs (after a gadget connected) shows the bit stuck.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/aspeed-vhub/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/aspeed-vhub/hub.c
@@ -533,9 +533,15 @@
 static void ast_vhub_send_host_wakeup(struct ast_vhub *vhub)
 {
 	u32 reg = readl(vhub->regs + AST_VHUB_CTRL);
-	UDCDBG(vhub, "Waking up host !\n");
-	reg |= VHUB_CTRL_MANUAL_REMOTE_WAKEUP;
-	writel(reg, vhub->regs + AST_VHUB_CTRL);
+	UDCDBG(vhub, "Waking up host (ctrl %08x) !\n", reg);
+	/*
+	 * Nothing ever cleared the manual remote wakeup bit: if the
+	 * hardware only acts on it going from 0 to 1, every wakeup after
+	 * the first one was lost. Make it an edge each time (harmless if
+	 * the hardware clears the bit itself).
+	 */
+	writel(reg & ~VHUB_CTRL_MANUAL_REMOTE_WAKEUP, vhub->regs + AST_VHUB_CTRL);
+	writel(reg | VHUB_CTRL_MANUAL_REMOTE_WAKEUP, vhub->regs + AST_VHUB_CTRL);
 }
 
 void ast_vhub_device_connect(struct ast_vhub *vhub,
@@ -846,6 +852,10 @@
 
 	vhub->suspended = false;
 
+	/* The wakeup (if it was ours) is done: the bit back to 0 */
+	writel(readl(vhub->regs + AST_VHUB_CTRL) & ~VHUB_CTRL_MANUAL_REMOTE_WAKEUP,
+	       vhub->regs + AST_VHUB_CTRL);
+
 	/*
 	 * Forward to unsuspended ports without changing
 	 * their connection status.
